# The application only creates CPU inference sessions, so onnxruntime-node must not download the
# CUDA and TensorRT execution providers it pulls from NuGet on linux/x64 by default. They unpack to
# more than a gigabyte and the OOM killer stops that in a default 1 GiB container.
# The deployment scripts and the image build pass ONNXRUNTIME_NODE_INSTALL=skip, which is the
# supported mechanism. This file repeats it for the one case those cannot reach: an already
# installed, older updater running npm ci on a new release. npm warns that it does not know this
# key, and if a future npm drops unknown project config, the environment variable still applies.
onnxruntime-node-install=skip
